    "legend": "Normal versus leukaemic B-cell immunophenotyping by flow cytometry. CD19+ B&nbsp;cells are a mixture of leukaemic B&nbsp;progenitors (red) and normal B&nbsp;progenitors (haematogones) showing complete maturation from stage&nbsp;I (cyan) to stage&nbsp;II (magenta) to stage&nbsp;III (orange) to mature B&nbsp;cells (green). Note the similarity of the leukaemia to the closest normal counterpart, stage&nbsp;I haematogones having bright CD10 and dim CD45, but with aberrant expression of CD9 (absent), CD10 (increased), CD20 (subset increased), CD22 (increased), CD34 (absent), CD38 (decreased), and CD58 (increased). The immunophenotypic abnormalities in comparison to the closest stage of normal maturation provide specificity for the diagnosis of neoplasia.",
